narrative:
## Building a Voting System

A real voting system needs three guarantees:
1. Only registered voters can vote
2. Each person votes exactly once
3. The count is always accurate

### Data Model

```xiom
let registered: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
let has_voted: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
let votes: Map[Str,Int] = Map[Str,Int].new();
```

- **registered** — who's allowed to vote
- **has_voted** — who already voted (prevents double-voting)
- **votes** — candidate name → vote count

### Registering Voters

```xiom
fn register(registered: Set[Str], name: Str) -> Bool {
  if registered.contains(name) { return false; }
  registered.insert(name);
  return true;
}
```

### Casting a Vote (with Contracts)

```xiom
fn cast_vote(
  registered: Set[Str],
  has_voted: Set[Str],
  votes: Map[Str,Int],
  voter: Str,
  candidate: Str
) -> Bool
  requires: registered.contains(voter);
  requires: !has_voted.contains(voter);
{
  has_voted.insert(voter);
  match votes.get(candidate) {
    Some(count) -> votes.insert(candidate, count + 1);
    None -> votes.insert(candidate, 1);
  }
  return true;
}
```

The contracts enforce the rules: only registered voters, no double-voting.

### Displaying Results

```xiom
fn show_results(votes: Map[Str,Int], candidates: Vec[Str]) {
  io.println("Results:");
  for c in candidates {
    match votes.get(c) {
      Some(count) -> io.println("  " + c + ": " + string.int_to_str(count));
      None -> io.println("  " + c + ": 0");
    }
  }
}
```

### Full Program

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let registered: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
  let has_voted: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
  let votes: Map[Str,Int] = Map[Str,Int].new();
  let candidates: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();

  registered.insert("alice");
  registered.insert("bob");
  registered.insert("charlie");

  candidates.push("Lee");
  candidates.push("Jordan");

  cast_vote(registered, has_voted, votes, "alice", "Lee");
  cast_vote(registered, has_voted, votes, "bob", "Jordan");
  cast_vote(registered, has_voted, votes, "charlie", "Lee");

  show_results(votes, candidates);
  io.println("Voters: " + string.int_to_str(has_voted.len()));
  return 0;
}
```

